<%#
    One channel picker: a <select> with an <option> per channel the bot can see.

    The five-line `channels.forEach` loop this replaces was copy-pasted into 28
    places across 20 panels (#671), so every fix to how an option renders — the
    escaping, the `#` prefix, how "selected" is decided — had to be made 28
    times or not at all. The panel partials were already used well; this is the
    same idea one level down.

    `channels` comes from the page's own locals, so no call site passes it.

    Locals, all optional, though a select wants either an `id` or a `cls`:

      id           the id its <label for=""> points at
      cls          a class instead of an id, for the repeater rows that are
                   addressed as a group and so cannot each carry one
      ariaLabel    a name for a select with no visible label of its own
      placeholder  text for a leading empty option; omit for none, which is
                   what a multi-select wants
      selected     the chosen channel id, or an array of them
      multiple     render a multi-select
      size         visible rows — only meaningful with `multiple`
      noDirty      mark it `data-no-dirty`: an "add one" picker feeding a chip
                   list is not itself a setting, and the unsaved-changes
                   tracking must not read it as one (#662)
-%>
<%_ const chosenChannels = new Set([].concat(locals.selected == null ? [] : locals.selected).map(String)); _%>
<select
<%_ if (locals.id) { _%>
 id="<%= locals.id %>"
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (locals.cls) { _%>
 class="<%= locals.cls %>"
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (locals.ariaLabel) { _%>
 aria-label="<%= locals.ariaLabel %>"
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (locals.multiple) { _%>
 multiple<% if (locals.size) { %> size="<%= locals.size %>"<% } %>
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (locals.noDirty) { _%>
 data-no-dirty
<%_ } _%>
><% if (locals.placeholder) { %><option value=""><%= locals.placeholder %></option><% } %><% channels.forEach(function (channel) { %><option value="<%= channel.id %>"<%= chosenChannels.has(String(channel.id)) ? ' selected' : '' %>>#<%= channel.name %></option><% }); %></select>
